course: dictionary
lesson: 7154
title: Perfectly: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Perfectly» has two main meanings. The first is in a perfect way, with no mistakes. «Picasso could draw perfectly at 15» means his drawings had no mistakes.
explain: The second meaning is completely or very. «A cat may sit perfectly still» means the cat is completely still, not moving at all. «It's perfectly safe» means it is completely safe.
explain: To find the right meaning, read the words after «perfectly». Then try swapping in «without mistakes» or «completely». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Perfectly means in a perfect way, without any mistakes.
fact: Perfectly also means completely or very, as in «perfectly safe» and «perfectly fine».
fact: «Perfectly still» means completely still, not moving at all.
fact: «Step counters are not perfectly accurate» means they can make mistakes, so they do not always count right.
fact: Perfectly often comes before another word to make it stronger, as in perfectly well or perfectly smooth.
exercise: «Picasso could draw perfectly at 15.» What does perfectly mean here? | Quite badly | *In a perfect way, without mistakes | Very slowly | Only sometimes
exercise: «A cat may sit perfectly still beside a hole in the garden.» What does perfectly still mean? | Moving slowly in circles | Asleep in the sun | *Completely still, not moving at all | Very fast
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Step counters are not perfectly accurate» that means exact and free from mistakes. | not | counters | *accurate | step
test: Maya says, «It's perfectly fine.» What does perfectly mean? | Quickly and loudly | Without any colour | Only a little fine | *Completely, with no problem at all
test: Why might a pupil say, «I know my times tables perfectly»? | They know only a few of them | They have never tried them | *They can answer every question without a mistake
exam: In «You know perfectly well», which meaning fits best? | *Completely or very | In a perfect way, with no mistakes | Only just | Quickly
